{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>If a man have.</b> Therefore these sections were juxtaposed here, to teach that one transgression drags another: because he takes a woman of fair appearance, he will have two wives, and strife in his house — and not only that, but he will hate the one. And what is written after it? כי יהיה לאיש בן סורר ומורה — for so we find with David: because he took the daughter of Talmai king of Geshur when he went out to war, Absalom came out of her, who sought to kill him and lay with his wives, and through him how many tens of thousands of Israel were killed. And what is written after it? וכי יהיה באיש חטא משפט מות — if he escapes from this, he will not escape from that. Thus transgression drags transgression."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:12.458454090Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}